# Reviewed, accepted-risk findings only - per docs/adr/0010, HIGH/CRITICAL
# with no upstream fix yet get a justified entry here, not a loosened gate.
# Re-evaluate whenever this file is touched: if Debian has since shipped a
# fix, remove the entry and let a rebuild resolve it instead.
#
# All eight are base-OS packages inherited from python:3.12-slim - none are
# in a code path the gateway application (FastAPI/uvicorn/httpx, running as
# a non-root user with no mount/cgroup capabilities) ever exercises.

# ncurses: buffer overflow in a terminal UI library never linked by the app
CVE-2025-69720

# systemd-homed: local privesc via home-dir daemon; homed never runs here
CVE-2026-16742

# libacl: symlink-traversal privesc via ACL functions; unused, non-root
CVE-2026-54369

# util-linux: four related CVEs needing mount/nsenter/CAP_SYS_ADMIN, which
# this container has none of (no mounts performed, no elevated caps)
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# perl-Archive-Tar: DoS via crafted tar; perl is a base-image package the
# Python application never invokes. Debian status is fix_deferred.
CVE-2026-9538

# openssl: a fix exists in Debian's own package repo (3.5.7-1~deb13u3) but
# the python:3.12-slim base image had not yet been rebuilt against it as
# of the digest pinned in the Dockerfile - checked directly against Docker
# Hub's tags API before writing this, not assumed. DoS via QUIC flow
# control / DTLS retransmission info disclosure - the gateway makes no
# QUIC or DTLS connections of any kind (httpx over plain HTTP/1.1 to vLLM).
CVE-2026-75804
CVE-2026-84782
